# GitHub sync (Prompt2Plan)

Remote repository: https://github.com/shalinibr001/Prompt2Plan  
Default branch: `master`  
Remote name: `origin`

Whenever you finish a meaningful code change in this project:

1. Stage relevant files (never commit secrets like `.env`, `.env.local`, credentials).
2. Commit with a concise message focused on why.
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if upstream is missing).
4. If push is rejected due to remote commits, pull with rebase (`git pull --rebase origin master`) then push again — do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks.

Do this without waiting for the user to ask, as long as the change is part of completing their request.
